#: ../../adr/0004-backend-selection.md:1
msgid "ADR-0004: Automatic backend selection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0004-backend-selection.md:3
msgid "**Status**: accepted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0004-backend-selection.md:4
msgid "**Date**: 2026-10-16"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0004-backend-selection.md:5
msgid "**Plan step**: P2.3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0004-backend-selection.md:7
msgid "Context"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0004-backend-selection.md:9
msgid ""
"REQ-HPC-2 asks LUMOS to detect the hardware it runs on and to pick the "
"array backend that exploits it best, while letting the user force a "
"choice. Several backends may be installed at once (NumPy always, JAX, "
"CuPy, PyTorch), with or without a GPU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0004-backend-selection.md:13
msgid "Decision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0004-backend-selection.md:15
msgid ""
"`lumos.config.backend` is `\"auto\"` by default; it can be set to any "
"backend name. `lumos.backend.use()` overrides it locally (per thread or "
"task)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0004-backend-selection.md:17
msgid ""
"With `\"auto\"`, the backend is chosen once per process, the first time "
"an array is needed, from `hardware_report(probe_gpus=True)` by the pure "
"function `select_backend`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0004-backend-selection.md:19
msgid "**JAX** if it sees a GPU (or TPU);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0004-backend-selection.md:20
msgid "otherwise **CuPy** if it sees a GPU;"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0004-backend-selection.md:21
msgid "otherwise **PyTorch** if it sees a GPU (CUDA, ROCm or Apple Metal);"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0004-backend-selection.md:22
msgid "otherwise **NumPy**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0004-backend-selection.md:23
msgid "The choice is logged (`INFO` level on the `lumos.backend._core` logger)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0004-backend-selection.md:25
msgid "Rationale"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0004-backend-selection.md:27
msgid ""
"JAX is the differentiable reference of LUMOS (decision D3): preferring it"
" on GPUs gives the same results, gradients included, as on a GPU-less "
"development machine running JAX on CPU."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0004-backend-selection.md:29
msgid ""
"Without a GPU, NumPy (with multi-threaded `scipy.fft`) is the reference "
"implementation, has no compilation overhead and no device transfer; JAX "
"on CPU stays available on request (`use(\"jax\")`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0004-backend-selection.md:32
msgid "Alternatives considered"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0004-backend-selection.md:34
msgid ""
"**Benchmark at start-up**: more accurate but slow and non-deterministic; "
"it may come later as an opt-in helper."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0004-backend-selection.md:36
msgid "**Always NumPy unless asked**: simpler, but contradicts REQ-HPC-2."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0004-backend-selection.md:38
msgid "Consequences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0004-backend-selection.md:40
msgid ""
"The first array operation of a process with `\"auto\"` imports the "
"installed GPU-capable libraries to list their devices (one-off cost of "
"about a second); importing `lumos` itself stays light."
msgstr ""

#: ../../adr/0004-backend-selection.md:42
msgid ""
"Results must not depend on the backend beyond floating-point tolerances; "
"the test suite is parametrised by backend to enforce it."
msgstr ""
